WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.552
Print and return are not the same thing.

00:00:03.552 --> 00:00:07.022
Print displays a value for a person to see.

00:00:07.022 --> 00:00:15.538
Return sends a value back to the rest of the program so it can be stored, formatted, or used in another calculation.

00:00:16.088 --> 00:00:23.130
A useful rule is: if the result will be reused later, return is usually the better choice.

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:26.997
This distinction becomes very important as programs grow.
